Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.

Question: Based on the 'multi-timed bring down provision' provided, when are representations and warranties required to be made?

Option A: Exclusively at Closing for all representations
Option B: At Signing for representations expressly marked 'as of Signing' and at Closing for all remaining representations

Merger Agreement: Section 9.3 Conditions Precedent for Completion. The obligations of the parties to consummate the Merger are subject to the following conditions: 
(i) Each of the representations and warranties contained in Articles IV and V, except those expressly designated as "as of Signing," shall be true and correct as of the Closing Date, as though made on that date; 
(ii) Any representation expressly marked "as of Signing" is deemed acceptable if it is true as of the execution date of this Agreement, regardless of its status at Closing; 
(iii) For any representations not explicitly time-stamped as "as of Signing," verification is only required at Closing, notwithstanding any interim updates provided by the Seller.

Determine the appropriate timing requirement for the representations and warranties based on the above provisions.
Choices:
